# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Scoped USB device policy for the Android Auto receiver (task 29, #133).
#
# SCOPE - narrow by construction. This file matches ONLY the approved phone /
# AOA accessory vendor:product identities, on ANY host USB port:
#
#     04e8:6860  Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra, phone / MTP mode
#     18d1:2d00  Android Open Accessory (AOA) mode
#     18d1:2d01  Android Open Accessory mode + ADB (post-switch enumeration)
#
# Any other vendor:product id on any port does not match. There is no
# vendor-wide, class-wide or hub-wide rule here, no system-wide ModemManager
# disable, and no rule for the keyboard/mouse dongle, the Bluetooth radio,
# hubs or the usb-serial class at large: unrelated devices keep default udev
# and ModemManager policy.
#
# NO PORT CONSTRAINT (#133, owner decision 2026-11-15): the policy used to pin
# KERNEL(S)=="1-2.1". A port adds no security - USB ids are spoofable, and a
# spoofing device can use the approved port as easily as any other - while it
# made an approved phone in another hub socket unusable. Trust is decided by
# the receiver's approved-phones store (serial-backed identities match on any
# port), never by this file: device-node access grants nothing on its own.
#
# WHAT IS APPLIED (to the matched device tree only):
#   1. ModemManager: ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1" on exactly the matched
#      device tree (usb device + its interfaces + its tty ports). Without it
#      ModemManager probes the phone's CDC-ACM ports ("couldn't check support
#      for device ...: not supported by any plugin"). The ATTRS id match +
#      ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE form follows ModemManager's own
#      77-mm-*-device-blacklist.rules convention. Every other device stays
#      visible to ModemManager.
#   2. Receiver session access to the accessory bulk-pipe node
#      (/dev/bus/usb/BBB/DDD): GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660",
#      TAG+="uaccess". plugdev + MODE 0660 + TAG uaccess is the project's
#      established Android-accessory ACL convention (tools/usb-policy/
#      README.md "Access control"); uaccess grants the active seat session
#      user and auto-revokes with the session; 0660 denies everyone else.
#      Least privilege: no MODE="0666", no world access, no class rules, and
#      the ACL applies to the usb_device node only (never interfaces/ttys).
#
# NUMBERING: 70- runs after 50-udev-default.rules (so MODE/GROUP for these
# exact device nodes take effect) and before 73-seat-late.rules (so
# TAG+="uaccess" is registered before the uaccess builtin applies the ACL)
# and before the 77-/80- ModemManager rules. It cannot override later system
# rules.
#
# ROLLBACK: tools/usb-policy/rollback.sh restores the exact prior state.
# See tools/usb-policy/README.md ("Rollback").
#
# ROLLBACK DOC + ops: tools/usb-policy/README.md

# --- ModemManager: ignore exactly the matched device tree -----------------
SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="04e8", ATTRS{idProduct}=="6860", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2d00", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2d01", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"

# --- Receiver session access to the accessory bulk-pipe node -------------
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="04e8", ATTR{idProduct}=="6860", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="2d00", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="2d01", GROUP="plugdev", MODE="0660", TAG+="uaccess"
